GuessLocationController:
  initialize()
    When called: Automatically by JavaFX after FXML loading.
    Purpose: Sets up the game state and map.
    Details:
      Loads the dataset of rounds from the CSV.
      Prepares the WebEngine (WebView) with console logging and a Java ↔ JS bridge.
      Ensures map initialization after page load and forces redraws to prevent “grey tiles.”
      Starts the first round.
  javaLog(String level, String msg)
    Purpose: Allows JavaScript console messages (console.log and console.error) to appear in the Java console for debugging.
    Usage: Called indirectly from injected JavaScript.
  nudgeRedraw(long delayMs)
    Purpose: Fixes WebView tile rendering issues.
    Details: Waits for a given delay, then calls refreshLeafletSize() on the JavaFX thread. Used after map load.
  refreshLeafletSize()
    Purpose: Tells Leaflet to recalculate its size and redraw tiles.
    Details: Calls the JS function window.forceRedraw()
  loadDataset()
    Purpose: Reads the CSV file (/data/guess_location.csv) and prepares the game rounds.
    Details:
    Each row → filename, latitude, longitude, optional label.
    Validates that image files exist.
    Creates Round objects and shuffles them.
    Throws an error if dataset is missing or empty.
  nextRound()
    Purpose: Advances the game to the next photo/location.
    Details: 
      Increments the round index.
      If all rounds are finished, shows final score and disables buttons.
    Otherwise:
      Displays new photo.
      Updates round and score labels.
      Resets guess and UI state.
      Prompts the user to drop a pin.
  onMapClick(double lat, double lon)
    Purpose: Called from JavaScript when the user clicks on the map.
    Details:
      Saves the clicked latitude/longitude.
      Update the feedback label to show selected coordinates.
  onSubmit()
    Purpose: Submits the user’s guess for the current round.
    Workflow:
      Validates that a guess exists and prevents duplicate submissions.
      Computes the distance between guess and ground truth using haversineKm.
      Assigns points (3, 2, 1, or 0).
      Updates score and feedback label with results.
      Calls JS function showResultLine(...) to draw markers and line.
      Disables Submit and enables Next.
  onNext()
    Purpose: Moves to the next round after a guess has been submitted.
    Details: Calls nextRound() only if the current round was answered.

  haversineKm(double lat1, double lon1, double lat2, double lon2)
    Purpose: Calculates the distance between two points on Earth in kilometers.
    Details:
      Uses the Haversine formula with Earth radius = 6371.0088 km.
      Returns great-circle distance (accurate for small and large distances).

  onSelectionScreen(ActionEvent event)
    Purpose: Navigates back to the “Selection Screen.”
    Details:
      Loads /fxml/game.fxml.
      Applies /css/style.css.
      Sets stage title to “Selection Screen.”
      Shows a new scene.

