map.html:
  forceRedraw()
    Purpose: Fixes a WebKit/JavaFX bug where map tiles sometimes remain grey.
    How it works:
      Calls map.invalidateSize(true) to force Leaflet to recalc tile layout.
      Calls a “no-op” pan (map.panBy([0,0])) which triggers a full repaint.
      Exposed as: window.forceRedraw so Java (refreshLeafletSize()) can call it.

  window.initMap()
    Purpose: Creates the Leaflet map instance after WebView has a real size.
    Details:
      Skips setup if window.map already exists.
      Creates map centered at [20,0], zoom level 2.
      Adds OpenStreetMap tile layer.
      Registers a click handler:
      Places/updates a marker at the clicked location.
      Calls window.app.onMapClick(lat, lng) (Java callback) to pass the coordinates back.
      Hooks window.addEventListener('resize', ...) to call forceRedraw() when WebView resizes.
      Logs Leaflet map size once to JS console (forwarded to Java console).

  window.showResultLine(fromLat, fromLng, toLat, toLng)
    Purpose: Called from Java to visualize the guess vs. the correct location.
    Details:
      Removes any existing polyline.
      Draws a new L.polyline between [fromLat, fromLng] (guess) and [toLat, toLng] (truth).
      Calls map.fitBounds() to zoom/center so both points are visible, with padding.
      Logs errors if something goes wrong.










